IMPORT prelude

-- Preservation of Monuments Act 2009 (Singapore) -- what the Act asks of the owner, occupier, buyer or contractor of a national
-- monument: notice of dealings (s 11(10), (11)), the dwelling-house saving (s 12), preservation notices and appeals (s 13),
-- works needing the Board's permission and their defences (s 15), information notices (ss 16, 17), enforcement notices and
-- appeals (ss 18 to 20), wilful defacing (s 22), the carve-out for Government and statutory authorities (s 22A), obstruction and
-- forcible entry (s 27(2A), (3)) and composition (s 31).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PMA2009.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the latest amendment annotated in
-- the text is [36/2021], the Preservation of Monuments (Amendment) Act 2021 (commenced 30 November 2021 per the Legislative
-- History). The retrieval record calls it the "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026".
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0129 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. SCOPED to the duties, offences, defences, deadlines and penalties an owner, occupier, buyer, contractor or member
-- of the public meets. Not encoded: the Board's functions and powers (ss 3 to 7), appointments (ss 8 to 10), how a preservation
-- order is made, amended or revoked and registered against title (s 11(1) to (9), (12)), entry powers beyond s 27(2A), arrest
-- (s 28), officers' liability for corporate offences (s 29), the Part 5 transfer from the old Preservation of Monuments Board,
-- the general exemption (s 32), service of documents (s 34), regulations beyond the s 35(3) fine cap, and transitional
-- provisions (s 36). Who pays for works done in default (ss 14, 20(1)(c)) is described in NOTES.md, not encoded.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Preservation of Monuments Act 2009 -- monuments`

DECLARE Status IS ONE OF
    `a national monument`
    `a proposed national monument`
    `an unprotected building`

GIVEN `the status` IS A Status
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the status is protected` IF
    CONSIDER `the status`
    WHEN `an unprotected building` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the higher of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `11(10), (11) -- notice to the Board of a sale, lease or other dealing`

-- s 11(10): "Any person who intends to transfer, assign, demise or otherwise deal with any proposed national monument, monument or
-- land affected by a preservation order must give to the Board -- (a) not less than 2 weeks' notice in writing of the intended
-- transfer, assignment, demise or dealing ...; and (b) written notice of the completion ... within 2 weeks of the completion
-- thereof." (11): contravention -- "a fine not exceeding $10,000". (Two weeks is taken as 14 days.)
GIVEN `days of notice before the dealing` IS A NUMBER, `days after completion that completion was notified` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dealing was properly notified` IF
        `days of notice before the dealing` AT LEAST 14
    AND `days after completion that completion was notified` AT MOST 14

GIVEN `the status` IS A Status, `days of notice before the dealing` IS A NUMBER, `days after completion that completion was notified` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dealing is an offence under section 11(11)` IF
        `the status is protected` `the status`
    AND (NOT (`the dealing was properly notified` `days of notice before the dealing` `days after completion that completion was notified`))

§§ `12 -- saving for a dwelling house`

-- s 12: where a preservation order is made for a structure "that appears to the Board to be occupied as a dwelling house" and not
-- vested in the Board or the Government, "if the structure is not acquired under the Land Acquisition Act 1966 within the period of
-- one year from the date of the preservation order, the preservation order ceases to have effect in relation to that structure."
GIVEN `occupied as a dwelling house` IS A BOOLEAN, `vested in the Board or the Government` IS A BOOLEAN, `acquired within one year of the order` IS A BOOLEAN, `one year has passed since the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the preservation order still protects the structure` IF
    NOT (    `occupied as a dwelling house`
         AND (NOT `vested in the Board or the Government`)
         AND (NOT `acquired within one year of the order`)
         AND `one year has passed since the order`)

§§ `13, 19 -- appeals to the Minister and whether a notice bites meanwhile`

-- s 13(3): against a preservation notice the owner or occupier may appeal "within 14 days of service on him or her ... or within
-- such longer period as the Minister may allow". s 19(1): the same 14 days for "any person aggrieved" by an enforcement notice.
-- The Minister's decision is final (ss 13(4), 19(3)).
-- s 13(5), 19(4): the notice "takes effect from the date specified ... despite any appeal ... that is pending", unless (ss 13(6),
-- 19(5)) the Minister, satisfied that delay will cause no danger or damage, directs that it "does not take effect until the
-- determination or abandonment of the appeal".
GIVEN `days after service` IS A NUMBER, `longer period allowed by the Minister in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is in time` IF
    `days after service` AT MOST (`the higher of` 14 `longer period allowed by the Minister in days`)

GIVEN `an appeal is pending` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister directed a stay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice is in effect` IF
    NOT (`an appeal is pending` AND `the Minister directed a stay`)

§§ `13(7) -- failing to comply with a preservation notice`

-- s 13(1): the owner AND the occupier must "take all reasonable measures to ensure that the national monument is properly
-- maintained at all times". (2) the Board may require works "at his or her own expense". (7) failure to comply: "a fine not
-- exceeding $20,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $200 for every day or part of a day
-- during which the offence continues after conviction." No imprisonment.
GIVEN `days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 13(7)` MEANS
    20000 PLUS 200 TIMES `days continued after conviction`

§§ `15(1), (1A) -- works that need the Board's prior written permission`

-- s 15(1): a person must not, "without the prior written permission of the Board", (a) "demolish, reconstruct, alter or make
-- additions to", (b) "repair, renovate, repaint or redecorate" a national monument or proposed national monument, or (c) "deposit
-- any waste material on or pollute or flood the land or site" on which it stands; (d) prescribed acts.
-- s 15(1A): on a national or proposed national monument "which is a site", a person must not without permission (a) clear, dig up,
-- excavate or cultivate any plant or tree; (b) extract, mine, quarry or interfere with earth, stone, sand or things evidencing human
-- activity; (c) destroy the relationship of a building and its environment; (d) "park or leave any vehicle or vessel"; (e)
-- "damage or enclose" it -- "knowing or reckless as to whether it is a national monument or proposed national monument".
-- Subsection (1) has no such mental element; (1A) does.
-- Visiting and photographing are in neither list: the encoding treats them as never needing permission. That is an inference from
-- the lists; s 15(1)(d) lets regulations prescribe further acts, and none was retrieved.
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    `demolishing part of it`
    `adding an extension`
    `repainting it`
    `repairing the roof`
    `dumping waste on its land`
    `clearing trees on the site`
    `digging on the site`
    `parking a car on the site`
    `enclosing the site`
    `visiting it`
    `photographing it`

GIVEN `the act` IS A Act
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is a section 15(1) work` IF
    CONSIDER `the act`
    WHEN `demolishing part of it` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `adding an extension` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `repainting it` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `repairing the roof` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `dumping waste on its land` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the act` IS A Act
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is a section 15(1A) site act` IF
    CONSIDER `the act`
    WHEN `clearing trees on the site` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `digging on the site` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `parking a car on the site` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `enclosing the site` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the act` IS A Act, `the status` IS A Status, `the monument is a site` IS A BOOLEAN, `had the Board's prior written permission` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew or was reckless as to its status` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act contravenes section 15` IF
        `the status is protected` `the status`
    AND (NOT `had the Board's prior written permission`)
    AND (    `the act is a section 15(1) work` `the act`
         OR  (    `the act is a section 15(1A) site act` `the act`
              AND `the monument is a site`
              AND `knew or was reckless as to its status`))

§§ `15(8), 22A -- defences and the carve-out for public bodies`

-- s 15(8): a defence if the person proves, on a balance of probabilities, the act was done (a) "urgently or immediately for the
-- safety of persons or property" AND "with all reasonable care" to have no more effect on its character or appearance "than was
-- necessary"; or (b) "in good faith" AND to comply with an order or requirement "of the Government or a statutory authority (other
-- than the Board)" under other written law.
-- s 22A: "Nothing in Part 4 applies" to the Government or a statutory authority (other than the Board) acting under written law
-- other than this Act in relation to a monument that is, or is on, "State land" or land vested in or under the care, control or
-- management of the Government or that authority.
DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    `a private owner`
    `a contractor`
    `the Government`
    `a statutory authority`
    `the National Heritage Board`

GIVEN `the actor` IS A Actor, `acting under other written law` IS A BOOLEAN, `on State or public land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 4 does not apply` IF
        `acting under other written law`
    AND `on State or public land`
    AND CONSIDER `the actor`
        WHEN `the Government` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a statutory authority` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `urgent for safety` IS A BOOLEAN, `with all reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN, `in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `complying with another authority's order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 15(8) defence is proved` IF
        (`urgent for safety` AND `with all reasonable care`)
    OR  (`in good faith` AND `complying with another authority's order`)

GIVEN `the actor` IS A Actor, `the act` IS A Act, `the status` IS A Status, `the monument is a site` IS A BOOLEAN, `had the Board's prior written permission` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew or was reckless as to its status` IS A BOOLEAN, `acting under other written law` IS A BOOLEAN, `on State or public land` IS A BOOLEAN, `urgent for safety` IS A BOOLEAN, `with all reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN, `in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `complying with another authority's order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is guilty under section 15(4)` IF
        `the act contravenes section 15` `the act` `the status` `the monument is a site` `had the Board's prior written permission` `knew or was reckless as to its status`
    AND (NOT (`Part 4 does not apply` `the actor` `acting under other written law` `on State or public land`))
    AND (NOT (`a section 15(8) defence is proved` `urgent for safety` `with all reasonable care` `in good faith` `complying with another authority's order`))

§§ `15(4), 20(2) -- penalties for unauthorised works and for ignoring an enforcement notice`

-- s 15(4) and s 20(2) are worded alike: "(c) in the case of an individual, to a fine not exceeding $100,000 or to imprisonment for a
-- term not exceeding 12 months or to both and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every
-- day or part of a day ... after conviction; or (d) in any other case, to a fine not exceeding $200,000 and ... a further fine not
-- exceeding $10,000" a day. A company can be fined twice as much; only an individual can be imprisoned.
-- ss 15(7), 20(3): the court is to have regard to "any financial benefit" accrued from the offence (not modelled).
-- s 15(5): the court may also order restoration at the offender's expense or payment of the cost of restoring (not modelled).
GIVEN `an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for unauthorised works or an ignored enforcement notice` MEANS
    IF `an individual`
    THEN 100000 PLUS 5000 TIMES `days continued after conviction`
    ELSE 200000 PLUS 10000 TIMES `days continued after conviction`

GIVEN `an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months for unauthorised works` MEANS
    IF `an individual` THEN 12 ELSE 0

§§ `16, 17 -- information notices`

-- s 17(1): an offence if, "at any time after the end of the period of 21 days beginning with the day on which an information notice
-- has been served", the person has not complied. (2) defence: "he or she did not know, and could not with reasonable diligence have
-- ascertained, the information required". (3) an offence to make a statement "he or she knows to be false or misleading in a
-- material particular" or "recklessly" to make one. (4) "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or ... imprisonment ... not exceeding 12
-- months or ... both" plus "$100 for every day or part of a day" after conviction.
-- The count includes the day of service, so day 21 is the last day to comply.
GIVEN `days counted from and including the day of service` IS A NUMBER, `has complied` IS A BOOLEAN, `could not have ascertained the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `non-compliance with the information notice is an offence` IF
        `days counted from and including the day of service` GREATER THAN 21
    AND (NOT `has complied`)
    AND (NOT `could not have ascertained the information`)

GIVEN `the statement is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew it was false` IS A BOOLEAN, `was reckless` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the statement is an offence under section 17(3)` IF
    `the statement is false or misleading in a material particular` AND (`knew it was false` OR `was reckless`)

GIVEN `days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 17` MEANS
    10000 PLUS 100 TIMES `days continued after conviction`

§§ `22, 27(3), 11(11), 35(3) -- other maximum fines`

-- s 22(1): "Any person who wilfully defaces, damages or otherwise interferes with" a national or proposed national monument --
-- "a fine not exceeding $30,000 or ... imprisonment ... not exceeding 6 months or ... both".
-- s 27(3): refusing access to, obstructing, hindering or delaying the Director or an Inspector, misstating information or failing a
-- lawful demand -- "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or ... imprisonment ... not exceeding 6 months or ... both".
-- s 35(3)(b): a regulation offence may carry no more than "$5,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, ... $100 for every day".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `not notifying a dealing`
    `ignoring a preservation notice`
    `unauthorised works by an individual`
    `unauthorised works by a company`
    `ignoring an information notice`
    `ignoring an enforcement notice as an individual`
    `wilful defacing`
    `obstructing an inspector`
    `a breach of regulations at the cap`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `not notifying a dealing` THEN 10000
    WHEN `ignoring a preservation notice` THEN 20000
    WHEN `unauthorised works by an individual` THEN 100000
    WHEN `unauthorised works by a company` THEN 200000
    WHEN `ignoring an information notice` THEN 10000
    WHEN `ignoring an enforcement notice as an individual` THEN 100000
    WHEN `wilful defacing` THEN 30000
    WHEN `obstructing an inspector` THEN 10000
    WHEN `a breach of regulations at the cap` THEN 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months for the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `unauthorised works by an individual` THEN 12
    WHEN `ignoring an information notice` THEN 12
    WHEN `ignoring an enforcement notice as an individual` THEN 12
    WHEN `wilful defacing` THEN 6
    WHEN `obstructing an inspector` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `27(2A) -- forcible entry without warrant`

-- s 27(1): entry is "at any reasonable time without warrant and without using force". (2A) "However", where the Director or an
-- Inspector "suspects on reasonable grounds that an offence under section 13(7), 15(4), 20(1)(a) or 22(1) has been or is being
-- committed" AND "is unable to enter, or is refused entry", they "may forcibly enter ... without warrant", including "by breaking
-- open any outer or inner door or window".
GIVEN `the suspected offence` IS A Offence, `suspects on reasonable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN, `entry refused or impossible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `forcible entry is allowed` IF
        `suspects on reasonable grounds`
    AND `entry refused or impossible`
    AND CONSIDER `the suspected offence`
        WHEN `ignoring a preservation notice` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `unauthorised works by an individual` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `unauthorised works by a company` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `ignoring an enforcement notice as an individual` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `wilful defacing` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `31 -- composition`

-- s 31(1): a prescribed compoundable offence may be compounded "by collecting ... a sum not exceeding -- (a) one half of the amount
-- of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; or (b) $5,000, whichever is the lower." (2) on payment "no further
-- proceedings are to be taken". Which offences are prescribed was not retrieved; the base maximum fine (without the daily
-- continuing-offence fine) is used.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that can be collected to compound it` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`the maximum fine for the offence` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000
